{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghv1sZy7yMr3RUHykYQY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For MnCl₂, **Dq ≈ 623 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 6 225 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 767 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3 140 cm⁻¹** (C/B ≈ 4.1). These come from the full d⁵ Tanabe–Sugano energy matrices, solved by trial-and-error interpolation by hand. I did not diagonalise the final matrices to check that the computed bands match the observed ones.\n\n**Model.** High-spin octahedral d⁵ has a ⁶A₁g ground state. All three bands are spin-forbidden transitions from ⁶A₁g to quartet states from the free-ion ⁴G term. All energies below are measured from ⁶A₁g. I wrote down the 3×3 ⁴T₁ and ⁴T₂ matrices partly from memory. I checked them by setting Dq = 0: both then give the correct free-ion energies, ⁴G = 10B+5C, ⁴P = 7B+7C, ⁴D = 17B+5C and ⁴F = 22B+7C.\n\n**1. The ⁴E band does not depend on Dq.**\n- ⁴A₁g/⁴E_g(G) lies at 10B + 5C.\n- So 10B + 5C = 23 370 cm⁻¹, which gives C = 4 674 − 2B.\n\n**2. The ⁴T₁g matrix.** The basis is t₂⁴e, t₂³e² and t₂²e³. Diagonal elements are −10Dq+10B+6C, 19B+7C and 10Dq+10B+6C. Off-diagonal elements are ⟨1|2⟩ = ⟨2|3⟩ = −3√2B and ⟨1|3⟩ = C. Its lowest root is set equal to 19 180 cm⁻¹.\n\n**3. The ⁴T₂g matrix.** Diagonal elements are −10Dq+18B+6C, 13B+5C and 10Dq+18B+6C. Off-diagonal elements are ⟨1|2⟩ = ⟨2|3⟩ = −√6B and ⟨1|3⟩ = −(4B+C). Its lowest root is set equal to 22 130 cm⁻¹.\n\n**4. Solving.** I substituted C = 4 674 − 2B. For each trial B, I found the 10Dq that makes det(M − E·1) = 0 at the observed energy, separately for each band:\n\n| B (cm⁻¹) | 10Dq from ⁴T₁ | 10Dq from ⁴T₂ |\n|---|---|---|\n| 750 | 6 265 | 6 185 |\n| 800 | 6 150 | 6 294 |\n| 768 | 6 224 | 6 227 |\n\nThe two bands give the same 10Dq at B ≈ 767 cm⁻¹, where 10Dq ≈ 6 225 cm⁻¹ and C = 4 674 − 2B ≈ 3 140 cm⁻¹. These values are typical for Mn²⁺ surrounded by chloride: weak field, with B reduced from the free-ion value of about 960 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 623, \"B\": 7